# Phase 2 iter 8 — gcc 15.x + section-level dead code elimination.
#
# -ffunction-sections / -fdata-sections put each function/data in its own ELF
# section.  -Wl,--gc-sections drops unreferenced sections at link time.  In an
# LTO build (already on, BR2_ENABLE_LTO=y) this is largely redundant for
# in-package dead code, but it does help cross-package: per-package libraries
# carry fewer never-called helpers into the final binary.  Should also shrink
# the rootfs slightly.
BR2_GCC_VERSION_15_X=y
BR2_TARGET_OPTIMIZATION="-ffunction-sections -fdata-sections"
# Note: Buildroot uses BR2_TARGET_LDFLAGS for runtime linker flags but does
# not have a clean "all packages add --gc-sections" knob.  Most packages
# already pass --gc-sections when *_GC_SECTIONS=y or via per-package overrides.
# For a quick experiment we rely on the BR default behavior — if the win is
# small we'll iterate.
